# Security & Data Protection Rules

## 1. Zero Password Leakage Policy
- Passwords (`password`, `password_hash`) MUST NEVER be included in API state payloads (`GET /api/state`, `POST /api/state`).
- `sanitizeStateForClient()` MUST be called on all outgoing state JSON objects before returning `res.json()`.
- Passwords MUST NEVER be stored in plain text in client state or `localStorage`.

## 2. SQL & XSS Injection Protection
- All database queries MUST use parameterized inputs (`?` placeholders).
- Input fields MUST be sanitized using `sanitizeInput()` from `src/utils/securityEngine.js`.

## 3. Brute Force Protection
- Failed login attempts are tracked per username.
- Lockout duration is set to **1 Minute (60 seconds)** after 5 consecutive failed attempts.
- Rate limiting is enforced at 60 requests per minute per session.

## 4. Environment Secrets Protection
- Secrets (`DB_PASSWORD`, `JWT_SECRET`) MUST be read exclusively from `process.env`.
- Hardcoding passwords or secrets in source code is strictly forbidden.
- Diagnostic logs MUST log only `DB_HOST`, `DB_PORT`, `DB_NAME`, `DB_USER`, `NODE_ENV` — NEVER `DB_PASSWORD`.
